{"name":"Pink Mirage","hex":"#f4ede9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"mirage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An optical phenomenon in which light is refracted through a layer of hot air close to the ground, often giving the illusion of a body of water.","An illusion."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause to appear as or like a mirage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mirage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mirage","blocks":[{"text":"A mirage is a naturally occurring optical phenomenon in which light rays bend via refraction to produce a displaced image of distant objects or the sky. The word comes to English via the French (se) mirer, from the Latin mirari, meaning \"to look at, to wonder at\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Farallon_Islands_at_inferior_mirage_no_mirage_and_superior_mirage.jpg/330px-Farallon_Islands_at_inferior_mirage_no_mirage_and_superior_mirage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirage","wikidata":"Q308762"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidat